- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/previewmaterial.html
- Summary (EN): The Preview Material node applies a standard preview material to incoming geometry so you can see how a material looks. With no geometry connected it creates a built-in proxy shape, and textures wired into its inputs override the material's layers.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Preview Material applique un matériau d'aperçu standard à une géométrie, avec un proxy intégré si rien n'est branché, et ses entrées remplacent les couches du matériau.

- Inputs meaning: ["geo (optional; a proxy is used if unwired)", "basecolor", "metalness", "specular", "spec_color", "roughness", "coat", "coat_color", "coat_roughness", "sheen", "sheen_color", "sheen_roughness", "emission", "emission_color", "opacity", "normal", "height", "transmission", "transmission_color", "sss_amount", "sss_color", "sss_radius"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: Geometry input, or a grid (Metadata) matching the input size and orientation", "UDIM List: tiles cooked for preview: Use Context, Explicit, Automatic or Disabled", "Geometry: proxy shape when no geo is wired: Grid, Sphere, Box, Tube, Torus or Shader Ball", "Translate / Rotate / Scale / UV Scale / Divisions: proxy placement, UV tiling and refinement", "Default Color and Tint With Cd: base colour when basecolor is unwired, optionally tinted by Cd", "Default and scale parameters (Metalness, Specular, Roughness, Coat, Sheen, Emission, Opacity): fallback values and scaling of incoming layers", "Normal Map Scale and Height Scale: normal and displacement strength; Height Scale is often needed because height maps range 0 to 1", "Index of Refraction: specular and transmission calculations"]

- Caveats: ["The geometry needs a uv attribute and ideally MikkT tangents, otherwise normal maps may display incorrectly.", "Transmission and subsurface parameters apply to Karma only.", "The USD parameters (Base Asset Path, Base Primitive Path) are for Solaris and not meant for artistic adjustment.", "The page does not state the internal name cop previewmaterial; the match rests on the page title and file name."]

